hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2823","**
Narrated to us Naṣr ibn ʿAlī, who said: We were informed by Wahb ibn Jarīr, who said: My father narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr narrated to me, from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān, from his uncle Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr, from his father Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim (RA), who said:

""During the pre-Islamic era (Jāhiliyyah), Quraysh would only depart from Muzdalifah, and they would say: 'We are the Ḥums; we do not leave the Ḥaram.' Thus, they abandoned the standing (wuquf) at ʿArafah.

I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the Jāhiliyyah standing with the people at ʿArafah on his camel. Then, when dawn broke, he would return with his people to Muzdalifah, where he would stand with them and depart with them when they did."""
